  "id": "differential-effect",
  "term": "differential effect",
  "definition": "Differential effect is the difference in how two forms of stimulation influence the same physiological response. In this source, it refers to the unequal impact of femoral nerve versus quadriceps muscle stimulation on soleus activity, especially the stronger excitatory effect of nerve stimulation on the H-reflex.",
